    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161">

                <pb facs="0283" n="207" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg207"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">411.60d Finnish Vessels/157</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Finnish Minister</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Järnefelt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-12">April 12, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On January 30, 1935, Dr. Sigurd von Numers,
                    Secretary of your Legation, and Mr. John G. Poore, handed to the Legal Adviser
                    of the Department what was described in your note of February 1, 1935, as a
                    complete record regarding the claim for the detention of thirteen Finnish
                    sailing vessels.</p>
                <p>On March 4, 1935, the Answer of the United States to the claim was handed, in
                    triplicate, to Dr. von Numers. On the fourth of this month, you delivered to the
                    Legal Adviser the Reply of the claimants to the Answer of the United
                        States.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d161-f1"/></p>
                <p>Please inform me whether the statements, arguments and conclusions set forth in
                    the Reply are to be regarded in their entirety as reflecting the views and
                    positions of the Finnish Government.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed>R. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Walton Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
